+// The console's Interlocked helpers disable interrupts (mtmsrd r13), do a lwarx / compare / stwcx.
+// and restore the interrupt state (mtmsrd). Here that took the global critical region's lock, which
+// every other thread that uses the region (the guest's, the GPU command thread, the kernel) then waited
+// behind, while all the region holds is loads, compares, branches and a store-conditional, which is a
+// compare-and-swap and atomic by itself. With the SDK's cvar guest_atomics_lock_free (the default) the
+// three macros below leave the lock alone: mfmsr reads "interrupts enabled", the two mtmsrd do nothing
+// more than set the MSR bits. Read once, so a thread cannot enter a region with the lock and leave it
+// without.
+inline bool ppc_regions_lock_free_() {
